## 6. AI Pipeline (Cloudflare Worker)

### Endpoint
`POST https://ai.tinytales.workers.dev/process`

Called as a **Hasura Action** — Hasura handles auth, the worker handles AI.

### Request
```json
{
  "audio_url": "https://storage.supabase.co/...",
  "child_names": ["Lachlan", "Ben"],
  "family_account_id": "uuid"
}
```

### Response
```json
{
  "narrative": "Lachlan discovered that he can make his shadow dance...",
  "tags": ["Discovery", "Funny"],
  "title": "Dancing with shadows"
}
```

### Pipeline Steps
1. Fetch audio file from Supabase Storage URL
2. Send to **OpenAI Whisper** (`whisper-1`) for transcription
3. Send transcript + child names to **Anthropic Claude** (`claude-sonnet-4-5`) for narrative + tags
4. Return structured response
5. Audio file is deleted from Supabase Storage after successful processing

### Claude System Prompt Template
```
You are a warm, empathetic writer helping a parent preserve a precious memory.

Given a raw voice transcript of a parent describing a moment with their child/children ({{child_names}}), produce:
1. A polished 2-4 paragraph narrative in first person, warm and personal. Do NOT invent facts. Retain all emotional truth.
2. A short title (5 words max)
3. 1-3 tags from this list only: Milestone, Funny, Heartwarming, Discovery, Birthday, Adventure, Creative, Friendship, Family

Respond ONLY with valid JSON: { "narrative": "...", "title": "...", "tags": ["..."] }
```

### Hasura Action Definition
```yaml
- name: processAudioTale
  definition:
    kind: synchronous
    handler: https://ai.tinytales.workers.dev/process
  request_transform:
    body:
      action: transform
      template: '{"audio_url": {{$body.input.audio_url}}, "child_names": {{$body.input.child_names}}, "family_account_id": {{$session_variables["x-hasura-family-account-id"]}}'
```

